Revision history for Rex-Rancher

{{$NEXT}}
  - New install_method => 'artifact' for server and agent: checksum-verified
    release download for the node's arch. Pinned versions are verified after
    install; a service that fails to start dies with its journal tail.
  - New install_server options version, node_name and disable (also taken by
    rancher_deploy_server). K3s now disables traefik/servicelb via
    config.yaml instead of installer flags; the default set is unchanged.
  - Without a token, install_server reuses the host's existing server token,
    so a re-run never rotates a live cluster's token. The token reaches K3s
    (server and agent) via config.yaml only, never the installer command line;
    config.yaml and registries.yaml are written 0600 root:root, re-runs too.
  - Document gpu => 1 with newer Rex::GPU versions (new "GPU hardware
    support" POD section): per-generation driver choice, passthrough VMs, and
    the deploy aborting after node preparation on unsupported GPUs or OSes.
  - Fix K3s Service/ClusterIP routing: with cilium enabled the server config
    wrote cni:none + disable-kube-proxy:true for both distributions, but
    Cilium's kube-proxy replacement is wired for rke2 only, so on K3s
    kube-proxy was disabled with nothing replacing it. These keys (and the
    rke2-ingress-nginx disable) are now gated to rke2; K3s keeps its own
    kube-proxy and default CNI. Extracted the pure _build_server_config for
    offline unit testing (t/server-config.t). RKE2 is the verified/supported
    distribution; K3s is documented as unverified and install_server warns on
    it (karr #5).
  - Warn loudly when the saved kubeconfig would still point at
    https://127.0.0.1: rancher_deploy_server now emits a warning (rather than
    silently saving an unusable file) when no server address can be derived
    (no tls_san / kubeconfig_server) or when the derived address is loopback
    (127.0.0.1, localhost, ::1). The file is still saved; only the silence is
    removed.
  - Pre-connect host-key scan for Rex::LibSSH >= 0.004, which now verifies
    the server host key against known_hosts (CWE-322 fix). New exported
    rancher_scan_known_hosts($host) runs ssh-keyscan locally and seeds the
    key before the first verified connect, so provisioning a fresh SFTP-less
    Hetzner box no longer dies with "host key is not in known_hosts". It
    keeps verification on rather than disabling strict_hostkeycheck, and is
    idempotent. Wired via a 'before ALL' pre-connect hook in
    eg/hetzner-gpu.Rexfile — the canonical operator pattern.
  - Fixed requirement details.
  - Document the supported distribution set: node preparation is verified on
    Debian, Ubuntu and RHEL/Rocky; openSUSE Leap / SLES is now marked
    unverified and unsupported (the base-package step falls through to Rex's
    generic pkg/zypper path and has never run on real SUSE hardware). No
    behaviour change — documentation only.
  - Add eg/DEPLOY-CHECKLIST.md, a stage-by-stage live-deploy verification
    checklist (host-key scan, node prep, GPU, install_server, kubeconfig
    patch, wait_for_api, Cilium, device plugin, untaint) covering both RKE2
    and K3s where they differ — the honest gate for a pipeline change, since
    the suite proves compilation only. README points at it. t/00-load.t now
    also compile-checks Rex::Rancher::K8s directly (was loaded only
    transitively). No behaviour change.

0.001     2026-03-29 04:21:30Z
  - Initial release
  - RKE2 and K3s server/agent installation with unified config interface
  - Node preparation (hostname, NTP, sysctl, kernel modules, swap disable)
  - Cilium CNI installation and upgrades (idempotent: safe to re-run)
  - Registry mirror configuration (registries.yaml) with live update support
  - Kubernetes API operations via Kubernetes::REST (no kubectl required):
    wait_for_api, deploy_nvidia_device_plugin, untaint_node
  - Full deploy pipeline in rancher_deploy_server:
    node prep -> GPU setup -> install -> kubeconfig save -> wait API -> Cilium -> device plugin
  - kubeconfig saved locally with 127.0.0.1 patched to real server address
  - Optional GPU support via Rex::GPU (gpu => 1, reboot => 1)
  - NVIDIA device plugin DaemonSet deployment with nvidia.com/gpu capacity polling
  - untaint_node for single-node clusters (removes control-plane/master taints)
  - DPkg::Lock::Timeout=120 on apt-get calls for fresh-boot resilience
  - Tested on Hetzner dedicated servers (Debian 13, Rocky Linux 10.1, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS)
  - Requires Rex::LibSSH for deployment to SFTP-less hosts (common on Hetzner dedicated)
  - Optional: Kubernetes::REST + IO::K8s for local K8s API operations

